Test: String Indexing
--------------------------------------
String: abc
s[1] = a
s[2] = b
s[3] = c

String literal indexing:
"hello"[1] = h
"hello"[2] = e
"hello"[5] = o

Edge cases - out of bounds:
s[0] =  (should be empty)
s[4] =  (should be empty)
s[100] =  (should be empty)
""[1] =  (should be empty)

Edge cases - negative indices:
s[-1] =  (should be empty)
s[-5] =  (should be empty)

Edge cases - non-integer indices:
s[1.0] = a (should work)
s[2.5] = b (should truncate to 2)
s[3.9] = c (should truncate to 3)

Edge cases - string indices:
s["1"] = a (should convert to 1)
s["abc"] =  (should be empty)

Edge cases - multiple indices:
s[1,2] =  (should be empty)

Comparison tests:
  "abc"[2] == "b" ✓
  "hello"[1] == "h" ✓
  "hello"[5] == "o" ✓
  "abc"[4] == "" ✓ (out of bounds)

Variable string indexing:
  str[1] = w
  str[2] = o
  str[3] = r
  str[4] = l
  str[5] = d

Empty string indexing:
empty[1] =  (should be empty)
empty[0] =  (should be empty)

Single character string:
single[1] = x
single[2] =  (should be empty)

Expression indices:
test[1+1] = b (should be 'b')
test[2*2] = d (should be 'd')
test[6-2] = d (should be 'd')
test[idx] = c (should be 'c')

String concatenation with indexing:
combined = helloworld
combined[1] = h (should be 'h')
combined[5] = o (should be 'o')
combined[6] = w (should be 'w')
combined[10] = d (should be 'd')

Unicode and special characters:
unicode[1] = c (should be 'c')
unicode[4] = é (should be 'é')
special[1] = a (should be 'a')
special[2] = 
 (should be newline)
special[3] = b (should be 'b')
special[4] = 	 (should be tab)

Boundary conditions:
boundary[1] = x (first char)
boundary[3] = z (last char)
boundary[length(boundary)] = z (should be 'z')

Zero and very large indices:
z[0] =  (should be empty)
z[-0] =  (should be empty)
z[999999] =  (should be empty)

String indexing in expressions:
  "test"[1] "est" == "test" ✓
  "abc"[2] "def" == "bdef" ✓

Nested string indexing:
nested[1][1] would be parsed as nested access

String indexing with variable indices:
str_var[idx_str] = e (should convert '2' to 2, get 'e')
str_var[idx_num] = l (should be 'l')

Very long string:
length(long_str) = 100 (should be 100)
long_str[1] = a (should be 'a')
long_str[100] = a (should be 'a')
long_str[101] =  (should be empty)
